/* ---------- Lecture notes for each branch ---------- */
const NOTES={
gen:{pts:['Total testing process: pre-analytical (most errors), analytical and post-analytical phases.','Quality management system: QC, EQA, document control, competency assessment, audit (ISO 15189 framework).','Uncertainty: every result has analytical (CVa) and biological (CVi) variation; reference change value = 2.77 × √(CVa² + CVi²) for 95% significance.'],ref:['westgard','tietz','clsi_gp41']},
hem:{pts:['Classify anaemia by MCV and reticulocyte count first, then confirm with the blood film and specific tests.','The blood film remains the key quality check for any analyser flag.','Benign ethnic neutropenia is common in people of African origin: avoid unnecessary investigations.'],ref:['dacie','hsieh']},
coag:{pts:['PT tests VII, X, V, II and fibrinogen; APTT tests XII, XI, IX, VIII, X, V, II and fibrinogen.','Pre-analytical errors (under-filled tubes, haemolysis, heparin contamination) are the commonest causes of abnormal results.','Mixing studies separate deficiency (correction) from inhibitors (no correction).'],ref:['dacie']},
chem:{pts:['Know the reaction principle, the interferences (haemolysis, icterus, lipaemia) and the traceability of each method.','Diagnostic thresholds (diabetes, CKD, MI) come from guidelines, not from reference intervals.','Critical values must be phoned and documented.'],ref:['tietz','ada','ckdepi','udmi4']},
endo:{pts:['Immunoassay pitfalls: biotin, heterophile antibodies, macro-forms, hook effect.','Timing matters: cortisol rhythm, pregnancy trimester, recent illness.'],ref:['tietz','fda_biotin']},
urine:{pts:['Urinalysis quality depends on fresh specimens and standardised centrifugation and viewing.','Integrate strip chemistry with microscopy before reporting.'],ref:['eug','cheesbrough1']},
para:{pts:['Malaria microscopy remains the reference for species, stage and density; RDTs do not replace it for parasitaemia.','Repeat stool examinations (3 samples) increase sensitivity for intestinal parasites.','Schistosomiasis intensity (eggs/10 mL) guides control programmes.'],ref:['who_malaria','who_schisto','cheesbrough1']},
micro:{pts:['Specimen quality (correct site, timing, transport, before antibiotics) determines the value of culture.','Use current CLSI or EUCAST breakpoints and QC strains for every AST.','Report and act on alert organisms (MRSA, ESBL, carbapenemase producers).'],ref:['cheesbrough2','clsi_ast','eucast']},
sero:{pts:['Know sensitivity, specificity and predictive values: a positive screening test in a low-prevalence population needs confirmation.','Paired sera showing a fourfold rise are stronger evidence than a single titre.'],ref:['who_hiv','who_typhoid','who_brucella']},
bank:{pts:['Positive patient identification at sampling and at the bedside prevents ABO-incompatible transfusion.','Antibody screening and AHG crossmatch detect clinically significant alloantibodies.'],ref:['aabb','bsh_pt']},
histo:{pts:['Fixation is the most important step: it cannot be corrected later.','Every special stain needs a known positive control processed in parallel.','IHC must be validated and run with positive and negative controls; pre-analytical variables (fixation time) affect predictive markers.'],ref:['bancroft','asco_cap']},
cyto:{pts:['Preparation quality (fixation, thickness, staining) limits interpretation more than the observer.','Learn the normal and reactive cells thoroughly before studying malignancy.'],ref:['gill','bethesda_cx']},
cpath:{pts:['Standardised reporting systems link each category to a risk of malignancy and management.','Always correlate with clinical and imaging data; use cell blocks and ancillary tests.','Cyto-histological correlation is the backbone of cytopathology quality assurance.'],ref:['bethesda_cx','bethesda_thy','paris','issfc','who_lung']},
mol:{pts:['Contamination control: one-way workflow, separate rooms or cabinets, UNG/dUTP systems, aliquoted reagents.','Every run needs positive, negative (NTC) and internal controls.','Analytical sensitivity (LoD) and specificity must be verified locally before clinical use.'],ref:['buckingham','miqe']}
};
